<p><m>\displaystyle{c}=</m> <fillin characters="7"/> mi</p>
<p>Round to 2 decimal places.</p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>2.68</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>We know two sides and the angle between them, so we can use the law of cosines to calculate the third side.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}^{{2}}={2.22}^{{2}}+{3.91}^{{2}}-{2}{\left({2.22}\right)}{\left({3.91}\right)}{\cos{{\left({41.3}^{\circ}\right)}}}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}^{{2}}={7.1742541367256}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}=\sqrt{{{7.1742541367256}}}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}={2.6784798182412}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}\approx{2.68}</m></p></solution>
